<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l}_{1})\!+\!\tau_{L}2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l}_{1})\!+\!\max\Big\{\tau_{L}\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(1\!+\!2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\Big)\!-\!\tau_{L}2B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)\bar{C}^{l+1}_{\mathcal{S}}}{S},0\Big\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l}_{1})\!+\!\tau_{L}2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l}_{1})\!+\!\max\Big\{\tau_{L}\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(1\!+\!2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\Big)\!-\!\tau_{L}2B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)\bar{C}^{l+1}_{\mathcal{S}}}{S},0\Big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p13.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p13.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality follows from Eq.(<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 2.2 Residual neural network and its dynamical system modeling ‣ 2 Notations and problem formulation ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>); the first inequality uses a similar proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, Theorem 12]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, Lemma 4]</cite>; the second inequality follows from Proposition <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <math id="S4.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\bar{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}\leq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\bar{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}\leq S</annotation></semantics></math> is dependent on data <math id="S4.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>; and the third inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem13" title="Lemma 13. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>, Lemma 4]</cite> together with the symmetric of the class <math id="S4.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{\mathrm{V}^{l}_{1,:}\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}):\ \mathrm{x}^{l}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{l},\|\mathrm{V}^{l}_{1,:}\|_{1}\leq B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow><mi>l</mi></msubsup><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathrm{V}^{l}_{1,:}\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}):\ \mathrm{x}^{l}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{l},\|\mathrm{V}^{l}_{1,:}\|_{1}\leq B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}=\min\{\sqrt{S}\frac{1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{2(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha+\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)},\bar{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}=\min\{\sqrt{S}\frac{1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{2(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha+\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)},\bar{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq l\leq L-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq l\leq L-1</annotation></semantics></math>. This truncation is introduced to ensure that the coefficients in the recursive inequality remain nonnegative, which is required for the application of the discrete Grönwall inequality. Then we get</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l+1}_{1})\!\leq\!\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l}_{1})\!+\!\tau_{L}2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l}_{1})\!+\!\tau_{L}\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(1\!+\!2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\Big)\!-\!\tau_{L}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}}{S}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l+1}_{1})\!\leq\!\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l}_{1})\!+\!\tau_{L}2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{l}_{1})\!+\!\tau_{L}\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(1\!+\!2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\Big)\!-\!\tau_{L}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}}{S},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq l\leq L-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq l\leq L-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}\leq\min\{\sqrt{S}\frac{1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{2(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha+\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)},S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l+1}\leq\min\{\sqrt{S}\frac{1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{2(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha+\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)},S\}</annotation></semantics></math>. By applying Grönwall’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> to the inequality above together with <math id="S4.SS2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{L}\cdot L=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{L}\cdot L=T</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex46X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{L}_{1})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{L}_{1})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big(\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{0}_{1})+\frac{\tau_{L}L\cdot B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}(1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(\tau_{L}L\cdot 2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big(\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{0}_{1})+\frac{\tau_{L}L\cdot B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}(1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(\tau_{L}L\cdot 2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex46Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\exp(\tau_{L}L\cdot 2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})\tau_{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\big(\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}}{\sqrt{S}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\exp(\tau_{L}L\cdot 2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})\tau_{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\big(\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}}{\sqrt{S}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex46Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big(\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{0}_{1})+\frac{TB_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}(1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big(\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{0}_{1})+\frac{TB_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}(1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex46Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex46Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})\tau_{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\big(\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}}{\sqrt{S}}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})\tau_{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\big(\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}}{\sqrt{S}}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">Due to the lemma in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, Lemma 26.11]</cite> and Eq.(<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Remark 3. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), we see</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex47X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex47X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{0}_{1})=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\max\{\|\mathrm{U}_{1,:}\|_{1},|\mathrm{a}_{1}|\}\leq B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\cdot\psi\!\circ\!(\mathrm{U}_{1,:}\mathrm{d}_{(s)}\!+\!\mathrm{a}_{1})\!\leq\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\frac{B_{\rm in}\sqrt{2\log(2n_{\mathrm{d}})}\!+\!1}{\sqrt{S}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝜺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msup><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">∘</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em">+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{0}_{1})=\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\max\{\|\mathrm{U}_{1,:}\|_{1},|\mathrm{a}_{1}|\}\leq B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\cdot\psi\!\circ\!(\mathrm{U}_{1,:}\mathrm{d}_{(s)}\!+\!\mathrm{a}_{1})\!\leq\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}\frac{B_{\rm in}\sqrt{2\log(2n_{\mathrm{d}})}\!+\!1}{\sqrt{S}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p14.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p14.5.1" class="ltx_text">It then follows from the above two inequalities that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E23X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{L}_{1})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{L}_{1})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\rm in}\sqrt{2\log(2n_{\mathrm{d}})}+1+T\cdot(1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\rm in}\sqrt{2\log(2n_{\mathrm{d}})}+1+T\cdot(1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E23Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})\tau_{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}}{\sqrt{S}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})\tau_{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}}{\sqrt{S}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p14.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p14.6.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, combining Eq.(<a href="#S4.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), Eq.(<a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>), and Eq.(<a href="#S4.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>), we complete the proof.
<span id="S4.SS2.p14.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.
Our approach is to transform the generalization problem of continuous dynamical systems into estimating the Rademacher complexity of discrete systems and to apply a convergence property from the discrete-time ResNet to the continuous-time ResNet.
As in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, we use the following definition to connect the discrete- and continuous-time learnable parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be a vector space. Partition the interval <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> subintervals <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{[t_{L}^{l-1},t_{L}^{l})\}_{l=1}^{L-1}\cup[t_{L}^{L-1},t_{L}^{L}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{[t_{L}^{l-1},t_{L}^{l})\}_{l=1}^{L-1}\cup[t_{L}^{L-1},t_{L}^{L}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{L}^{l}:=l\cdot T/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{L}^{l}:=l\cdot T/L</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define a sampling operator <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}:\mathcal{C}([0,T];\mathcal{X})\rightarrow\mathcal{X}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓣</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}:\mathcal{C}([0,T];\mathcal{X})\rightarrow\mathcal{X}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Xi}\in\mathcal{C}([0,T];\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚵</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Xi}\in\mathcal{C}([0,T];\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Xi})=\big(\boldsymbol{\Xi}(t_{L}^{0}),\ldots,\boldsymbol{\Xi}(t_{L}^{L-1})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓣</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚵</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝚵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝚵</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Xi})=\big(\boldsymbol{\Xi}(t_{L}^{0}),\ldots,\boldsymbol{\Xi}(t_{L}^{L-1})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and define a piecewise constant extension operator <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}:\mathcal{X}^{L}\rightarrow\mathcal{M}_{L}([0,T];\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}:\mathcal{X}^{L}\rightarrow\mathcal{M}_{L}([0,T];\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{\Xi}_{L}=(\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{0},\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{1},\ldots,\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{L-1})\in\mathcal{X}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{\Xi}_{L}=(\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{0},\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{1},\ldots,\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{L-1})\in\mathcal{X}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\mathrm{\Xi}_{L})(t)=\sum_{l=0}^{L-2}\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{l}\boldsymbol{1}_{[t_{L}^{l},t_{L}^{l+1})}(t)+\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{L-1}\boldsymbol{1}_{[t_{L}^{L-1},t_{L}^{L}]}(t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\mathrm{\Xi}_{L})(t)=\sum_{l=0}^{L-2}\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{l}\boldsymbol{1}_{[t_{L}^{l},t_{L}^{l+1})}(t)+\mathrm{\xi}_{L}^{L-1}\boldsymbol{1}_{[t_{L}^{L-1},t_{L}^{L}]}(t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{L}([0,T];\mathcal{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{L}([0,T];\mathcal{X})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the space of piecewise constant functions on <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> pieces.
<span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using the above definition, we derive a convergence property between the state variables of discrete- and continuous-time ResNets.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 15</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let assumptions <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A_{1})-(A_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A_{1})-(A_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> hold and denote <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{L}^{l}=l\tau_{L}=l\cdot\frac{T}{L},0\leq l\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{L}^{l}=l\tau_{L}=l\cdot\frac{T}{L},0\leq l\leq L</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a learnable parameter <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}=({\Theta}^{\rm pre},{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}=({\Theta}^{\rm pre},{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}}</annotation></semantics></math> and input <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{d}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{\mathrm{d}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{d}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{\mathrm{d}}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{d}\|_{\infty}\leq B_{\rm in}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>in</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{d}\|_{\infty}\leq B_{\rm in}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then there exists a parameter <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}=({\Theta}^{\rm pre},{{\Theta}}_{L})\in\Omega_{{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}=({\Theta}^{\rm pre},{{\Theta}}_{L})\in\Omega_{{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a constant <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}{{\Theta}}_{L}-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}\leq C_{1}\tau_{L}^{1/2}\rightarrow 0\text{ as }L\rightarrow\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}{{\Theta}}_{L}-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}\leq C_{1}\tau_{L}^{1/2}\rightarrow 0\text{ as }L\rightarrow\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem15.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, for this <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{1\leq l\leq L}\sup_{t\in[t_{L}^{l-1},t_{L}^{l}]}\|\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})-\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\|_{\infty}\leq C_{2}\tau_{L}^{1/2}\rightarrow 0\ {\rm as}\ L\rightarrow\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>as</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{1\leq l\leq L}\sup_{t\in[t_{L}^{l-1},t_{L}^{l}]}\|\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})-\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\|_{\infty}\leq C_{2}\tau_{L}^{1/2}\rightarrow 0\ {\rm as}\ L\rightarrow\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem15.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">The proof primarily follows the approach in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>.
For every <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}=({\Theta}^{\rm pre},{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}=({\Theta}^{\rm pre},{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}=({\Theta}^{\rm pre},{{\Theta}}_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}=({\Theta}^{\rm pre},{{\Theta}}_{L})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{{\Theta}}_{L}=({{\Theta}}_{L}^{0},{{\Theta}}_{L}^{1},\ldots,{{\Theta}}_{L}^{L-1}):=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓣</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{{\Theta}}_{L}=({{\Theta}}_{L}^{0},{{\Theta}}_{L}^{1},\ldots,{{\Theta}}_{L}^{L-1}):=\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta})</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a similar proof of Morrey’s inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>, Remark 11.35]</cite>, we have for every <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,\hat{t}\in[0,T]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,\hat{t}\in[0,T]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}(t)-\boldsymbol{\Theta}(\hat{t})\|_{\infty}\leq\bar{C}_{1}|t-\hat{t}|^{1/2}\|D(\boldsymbol{\Theta})\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}\leq\bar{C}_{1}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}|t-\hat{t}|^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}(t)-\boldsymbol{\Theta}(\hat{t})\|_{\infty}\leq\bar{C}_{1}|t-\hat{t}|^{1/2}\|D(\boldsymbol{\Theta})\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}\leq\bar{C}_{1}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}|t-\hat{t}|^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\boldsymbol{\Theta}_{L}-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\boldsymbol{\Theta}_{L}-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\int_{t_{L}^{l}}^{t_{L}^{l+1}}\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}(t_{L}^{l})-\boldsymbol{\Theta}(t)\|_{\infty}^{2}dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\int_{t_{L}^{l}}^{t_{L}^{l+1}}\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}(t_{L}^{l})-\boldsymbol{\Theta}(t)\|_{\infty}^{2}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\int_{t_{L}^{l}}^{t_{L}^{l+1}}\bar{C}_{1}^{2}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}|t_{L}^{l}-{t}|dt\leq C_{1}^{2}\tau_{L}\rightarrow 0,\ L\rightarrow\infty," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{l=0}^{L-1}\int_{t_{L}^{l}}^{t_{L}^{l+1}}\bar{C}_{1}^{2}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}|t_{L}^{l}-{t}|dt\leq C_{1}^{2}\tau_{L}\rightarrow 0,\ L\rightarrow\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}\bar{C}_{1}^{2}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}\bar{C}_{1}^{2}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We next prove (<a href="#S4.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ Lemma 15. ‣ 4.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) for a such <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{L}^{l}=\|\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})-\mathbb{x}(t_{L}^{l};\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{L}^{l}=\|\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})-\mathbb{x}(t_{L}^{l};\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the ResNets defined in Eq.(<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 2.2 Residual neural network and its dynamical system modeling ‣ 2 Notations and problem formulation ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and Eq.(<a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ 2.2 Residual neural network and its dynamical system modeling ‣ 2 Notations and problem formulation ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) are special cases of the ResNet architectures considered in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Eq.(5) and Eq.(7)]</cite>, it follows from the proof of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite> that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{0\leq l\leq L}e^{l}_{L}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{0\leq l\leq L}e^{l}_{L}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\gamma_{L}M_{2}}{2}T\Big(1+\frac{M_{1}T}{L}\Big)^{2L}+\frac{M_{2}}{2\gamma_{L}}\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}-\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\boldsymbol{\Theta}_{L}\|^{2}_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}\!+\!M_{3}\frac{T^{2}}{L}\Big(1+\frac{M_{1}T}{L}\Big)^{L}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\gamma_{L}M_{2}}{2}T\Big(1+\frac{M_{1}T}{L}\Big)^{2L}+\frac{M_{2}}{2\gamma_{L}}\|\boldsymbol{\Theta}-\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\boldsymbol{\Theta}_{L}\|^{2}_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}\!+\!M_{3}\frac{T^{2}}{L}\Big(1+\frac{M_{1}T}{L}\Big)^{L},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{1},M_{2},M_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{1},M_{2},M_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are constants depending on <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}},B_{\rm in},T,\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}},B_{\rm in},T,\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{L}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{L}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> can be any constant. Taking <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{L}=\|\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\boldsymbol{\Theta}_{L}-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{L}=\|\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\boldsymbol{\Theta}_{L}-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}</annotation></semantics></math> and by Eq.(<a href="#S4.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), we get</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{0\leq l\leq L}\|\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})-\mathbb{x}(t_{L}^{l};\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\|_{\infty}\leq M_{4}\tau_{L}^{1/2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{0\leq l\leq L}\|\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})-\mathbb{x}(t_{L}^{l};\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\|_{\infty}\leq M_{4}\tau_{L}^{1/2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant dependent on <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}},B_{\rm in},T,\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}},B_{\rm in},T,\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E27X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E27X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\Big\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})}{\mathrm{d}t}\Big\|_{\infty}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\Big\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})}{\mathrm{d}t}\Big\|_{\infty}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E27X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\|\mathbb{W}(t)\psi\circ(\mathbb{V}(t)\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})+\mathbb{b}(t))+\mathbb{c}(t)\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕎</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝕩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝕔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\|\mathbb{W}(t)\psi\circ(\mathbb{V}(t)\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})+\mathbb{b}(t))+\mathbb{c}(t)\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E27Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E27Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E27Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}(B_{\rm out}+1)+B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}=:\mathrm{Lip}_{\mathbb{x}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>𝕩</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2}(B_{\rm out}+1)+B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}=:\mathrm{Lip}_{\mathbb{x}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\rm out}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\rm out}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant given in Lemma <a href="#S4.Ex23" title="Lemma 12. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.
Therefore, combining Eq.(<a href="#S4.E26" title="Equation 26 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and Eq.(<a href="#S4.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[t_{L}^{l-1},t_{L}^{l}]}\|\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})-\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[t_{L}^{l-1},t_{L}^{l}]}\|\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})-\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E28Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[t_{L}^{l-1},t_{L}^{l}]}\big(\|\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})-\mathbb{x}(t_{L}^{l};\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\|_{\infty}+\|\mathbb{x}(t_{L}^{l};\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})-\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\|_{\infty}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo mathsize="1.200em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{t\in[t_{L}^{l-1},t_{L}^{l}]}\big(\|\mathbb{x}(t;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})-\mathbb{x}(t_{L}^{l};\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\|_{\infty}+\|\mathbb{x}(t_{L}^{l};\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})-\mathrm{x}^{l}(\mathrm{d};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\|_{\infty}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E28Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E28Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Lip}_{\mathbb{x}}\tau_{L}+M_{4}\tau_{L}^{1/2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>𝕩</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Lip}_{\mathbb{x}}\tau_{L}+M_{4}\tau_{L}^{1/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Letting <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}=\mathrm{Lip}_{\mathbb{x}}\sqrt{T}+M_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>𝕩</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>T</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}=\mathrm{Lip}_{\mathbb{x}}\sqrt{T}+M_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
<span id="S4.SS3.p5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">(Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>)
We divide the proof into two steps.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Step 1. We show the boundedness of the loss function and apply the theorem in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, Theorem 26.5]</cite> to get a Rademacher complexity upper bound of the generalization gap.
Similar to the discussion in the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>,
the loss function <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by a constant <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> dependent on <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,B_{\rm in},B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}},\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,B_{\rm in},B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}},\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for any <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="S4.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="GE_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}))\leq 2\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\ell}\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T})+4B_{\ell}\sqrt{\frac{2\log(4/\delta)}{S}},\ \forall\ \mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in\mathcal{F}^{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">GE_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}))\leq 2\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\ell}\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T})+4B_{\ell}\sqrt{\frac{2\log(4/\delta)}{S}},\ \forall\ \mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in\mathcal{F}^{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">due to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>, Theorem 26.5]</cite>. Here <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\ell}\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T}=\{{f}(\cdot,\cdot)={\ell}(\mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\cdot):\ \mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\ell}\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T}=\{{f}(\cdot,\cdot)={\ell}(\mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\cdot):\ \mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Step 2. We estimate the Rademacher complexity <math id="S4.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\ell}\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\ell}\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to the discussion in Step 2 of the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.E30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E30X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\ell}\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\ell}\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\ell\circ\mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in\ell\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\cdot{\ell}(\mathbb{x}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝜺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\ell\circ\mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in\ell\circ{\mathcal{F}}^{T}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\cdot{\ell}(\mathbb{x}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E30Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\cdot{\ell}(\mathbb{x}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝜺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝕩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\mathbb{x}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\cdot{\ell}(\mathbb{x}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E30Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{2}B_{\kappa}\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}\sup_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k}\end{subarray}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\epsilon_{(sk)}\cdot\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕩</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em" rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo mathsize="0.710em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝕩</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{2}B_{\kappa}\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}}\sup_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k}\end{subarray}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\epsilon_{(sk)}\cdot\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E30Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{2}B_{\kappa}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{k,:}}\sup_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k}\end{subarray}}\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\epsilon_{(sk)}\cdot\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>κ</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕩</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em" rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo mathsize="0.710em">,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msup><mi>ϵ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕩</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{2}B_{\kappa}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{k,:}}\sup_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k}\end{subarray}}\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\epsilon_{(sk)}\cdot\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E30Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E30Xd.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{2}B_{\kappa}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathcal{F}^{T}_{k})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{2}B_{\kappa}\sum_{k=1}^{n}\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}(\mathcal{F}^{T}_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="S4.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{k,:}=\{\epsilon_{1k},\ldots,\epsilon_{Sk}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>:</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\epsilon}_{k,:}=\{\epsilon_{1k},\ldots,\epsilon_{Sk}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the first inequality is due to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>, Corollary 1]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">To apply the result in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we let <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{L}^{l}=l\tau_{L}=l\cdot\frac{T}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{L}^{l}=l\tau_{L}=l\cdot\frac{T}{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq l\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq l\leq L</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then there are constants <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},c_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},c_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta})-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|^{2}_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}\leq c_{1}\tau_{L},\forall\ \boldsymbol{\Theta}\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓘</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓣</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">∀</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{\boldsymbol{\mathcal{I}}}_{L}\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta})-\boldsymbol{\Theta}\|^{2}_{\mathcal{L}^{2}([0,T];\mathcal{E})}\leq c_{1}\tau_{L},\forall\ \boldsymbol{\Theta}\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">and also</span></p>
<table id="S4.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbb{x}(T;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})-\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d};({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta})))\|_{\infty}\leq c_{2}\tau^{\frac{1}{2}}_{L},\forall\mathrm{d}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{\mathrm{d}}},\forall\boldsymbol{\Theta}\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝕩</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>;</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓣</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>τ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></msup><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbb{x}(T;\mathrm{d};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})-\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d};({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta})))\|_{\infty}\leq c_{2}\tau^{\frac{1}{2}}_{L},\forall\mathrm{d}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{\mathrm{d}}},\forall\boldsymbol{\Theta}\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">by using Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem15" title="Lemma 15. ‣ 4.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>. Hence, noting <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta}))\in\Omega_{{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓣</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta}))\in\Omega_{{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\Theta})\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\Theta})\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying Eq.(<a href="#S4.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) and Eq.(<a href="#S4.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>), we get</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝜺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕩</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕩</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\cdot;\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})\in{\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\mathbb{x}_{k}(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\Big[\sup_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{\rm total}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\Big(\mathbb{x}_{k}\big(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}\big)-\mathrm{x}_{k}^{L}\big(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta}))\big)\Big)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝜺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕩</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓣</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\Big[\sup_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{\rm total}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\Big(\mathbb{x}_{k}\big(T;\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}\big)-\mathrm{x}_{k}^{L}\big(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta}))\big)\Big)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{\rm total}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\mathrm{x}_{k}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝜺</mi></msub><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>pre</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓣</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}\in\Omega_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{\rm total}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\mathrm{x}_{k}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};({\Theta}^{\rm pre},\boldsymbol{\mathcal{T}}_{L}(\boldsymbol{\Theta})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{c_{2}\sqrt{\tau_{L}}}+\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\mathrm{x}^{L}_{k}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\in\mathcal{F}_{k}^{L}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\mathrm{x}_{k}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝜺</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{c_{2}\sqrt{\tau_{L}}}+\frac{1}{S}\mathbb{E}_{\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}}\sup_{\mathrm{x}^{L}_{k}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\in\mathcal{F}_{k}^{L}}\sum_{s=1}^{S}\varepsilon_{(s)}\mathrm{x}_{k}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{c_{2}\sqrt{\tau_{L}}}+\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{L}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{c_{2}\sqrt{\tau_{L}}}+\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{L}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{c_{2}\sqrt{\tau_{L}}}+\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\rm in}\sqrt{2\log(2n_{\mathrm{d}})}+1+T(1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{c_{2}\sqrt{\tau_{L}}}+\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\rm in}\sqrt{2\log(2n_{\mathrm{d}})}+1+T(1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})\tau_{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}}{\sqrt{S}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\exp(2T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})\tau_{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\frac{(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta){C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}}{\sqrt{S}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}\leq\min\{\sqrt{S}\frac{1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{2(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha+\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)},S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>l</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq{C}_{\mathcal{S}}^{l}\leq\min\{\sqrt{S}\frac{1+2\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{2(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha+\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)},S\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{L}=\frac{T}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{L}=\frac{T}{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, letting <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, possibly along a subsequence, we conclude that there exists a constant <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> dependent on data <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex60X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex60X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℛ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{R}_{\mathcal{S}}({\mathcal{F}}^{T}_{k})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex60X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\rm in}\sqrt{2\log(2n_{\mathrm{d}})}+1+T(1+\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>in</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\sqrt{S}}\Big(\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\rm in}\sqrt{2\log(2n_{\mathrm{d}})}+1+T(1+\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}})\Big)\exp(T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex60Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex60Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)\exp(T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})T}{S}C_{\mathcal{S}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}(\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha\!+\!\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta)\exp(T\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}^{2})T}{S}C_{\mathcal{S}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq C_{\mathcal{S}}\leq\min\{\sqrt{S}\frac{1+\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha+\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta},S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>𝚯</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Lip</mi><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq C_{\mathcal{S}}\leq\min\{\sqrt{S}\frac{1+\mathrm{Lip}_{\psi}B_{\boldsymbol{\Theta}}}{\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{1}}\alpha+\mathrm{Lip}_{\phi_{2}}\beta},S\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting the above inequality into Eq.(<a href="#S4.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) and combining Eq.(<a href="#S4.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ 4 Proofs ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) completes the proof.
<span id="S4.SS3.p11.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we conduct experiments to evaluate the generalization ability of ResNets within the dynamical system modeling framework. Specifically, we examine how generalization is affected by varying the number of training samples and the number of neural network layers. We also investigate the influence of activation functions on the generalization behavior of ResNets from the perspective of the proposed theoretical framework.
All ResNets are trained for 30 epochs on the MNIST dataset and 120 epochs on the CIFAR10 and CIFAR100 datasets using the SGD optimizer with an initial learning rate of 0.01 and a momentum of 0.9.
All training and testing procedures are implemented using PyTorch on NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3090 GPUs. Our code is available at “<a href="https://github.com/Huangjsh15/Dynamical-ResNet.git" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">https://github.com/Huangjsh15/Dynamical-ResNet.git</a>”.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>A test on the influence of training sample size <math id="S5.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume that <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathfrak{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathfrak{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a large number such that <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathfrak{D}}\gg S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub><mo>≫</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathfrak{D}}\gg S</annotation></semantics></math>. Let the training and testing samples used in experiments be <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{(\mathrm{d}_{(s)},\mathrm{g}_{(s)})\}_{s=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{(\mathrm{d}_{(s)},\mathrm{g}_{(s)})\}_{s=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathcal{S}}=\{(\mathrm{d}_{(s)},\mathrm{g}_{(s)})\}_{s=S+1}^{S+\bar{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathcal{S}}=\{(\mathrm{d}_{(s)},\mathrm{g}_{(s)})\}_{s=S+1}^{S+\bar{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Following the definition of the generalization gap in (<a href="#S2.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 2.3 The problem of generalization for discrete- and continuous-time ResNets ‣ 2 Notations and problem formulation ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), we derive</p>
<table id="S5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle GE_{\mathcal{S}}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\big)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle GE_{\mathcal{S}}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\big)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\mathfrak{R}_{{\mathfrak{D}}}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\big)-\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\mathcal{S}}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\big)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℜ</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\mathfrak{R}_{{\mathfrak{D}}}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\big)-\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\mathcal{S}}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\big)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\approx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\approx}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}\sum_{s=1}^{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)-\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}\sum_{s=1}^{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)-\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\!\frac{S_{\mathfrak{D}}\!-\!S}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}\frac{1}{S}\!\sum_{s=1}^{S}\!{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\!\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)\!+\!\frac{S_{\mathfrak{D}}\!-\!S}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}\frac{1}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}\!-\!S}\!\sum_{s=S\!+\!1}^{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}\!{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\!\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>;</mo></mpadded><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.102em">+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mpadded style="width:0.275em;" width="0.275em"><mo>;</mo></mpadded><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\!\frac{S_{\mathfrak{D}}\!-\!S}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}\frac{1}{S}\!\sum_{s=1}^{S}\!{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\!\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)\!+\!\frac{S_{\mathfrak{D}}\!-\!S}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}\frac{1}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}\!-\!S}\!\sum_{s=S\!+\!1}^{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}\!{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\!\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex64.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{S_{\mathfrak{D}}-S}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}(\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}-\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train})\approx\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}-\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>test</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>train</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>test</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>train</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{S_{\mathfrak{D}}-S}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}(\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}-\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train})\approx\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}-\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the training loss <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train}\!=\!\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\mathcal{S}}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\big)\!=\!\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}{\ell}(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>train</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>total</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train}\!=\!\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\mathcal{S}}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\cdot;{\Theta}^{\rm total}_{L})\big)\!=\!\frac{1}{S}\sum_{s=1}^{S}{\ell}(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)})</annotation></semantics></math> and testing loss <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}\!=\!\frac{1}{\bar{S}}\sum_{s=S+1}^{\bar{S}+S}{\ell}(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)})\approx\frac{1}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}\!-\!S}\sum_{s=S+1}^{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.102em" rspace="0.102em">−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>𝔇</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝚯</mi><mi>total</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}\!=\!\frac{1}{\bar{S}}\sum_{s=S+1}^{\bar{S}+S}{\ell}(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)})\approx\frac{1}{S_{\mathfrak{D}}\!-\!S}\sum_{s=S+1}^{S_{\mathfrak{D}}}{\ell}\big(\mathrm{x}^{L}(\mathrm{d}_{(s)};\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\rm total}),\mathrm{g}_{(s)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> since we assume the samples are i.i.d. distributed.
This derivation shows that the difference between the testing and training losses can approximate the generalization gap (<a href="#S2.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 2.3 The problem of generalization for discrete- and continuous-time ResNets ‣ 2 Notations and problem formulation ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). Therefore, the result in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> can be empirically validated by measuring the quantity <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}\!-\!\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>test</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>train</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}\!-\!\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train}</annotation></semantics></math> under varying training sample size <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In Figure <a href="#S5.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 5.1 A test on the influence of training sample size 𝑆 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we present the average testing-training loss gap of ResNets <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}-\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>test</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>train</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm test}-\hat{\mathfrak{R}}_{\rm train}</annotation></semantics></math> at the last 10 epochs for ResNets trained on the MNIST, CIFAR10, and CIFAR100 datasets.
Guided by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, which suggests an <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\frac{1}{\sqrt{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\frac{1}{\sqrt{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> generalization rate, we fit the empirical gap using the least squares method with function <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{h}_{\mu}(S)=\mu/\sqrt{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{h}_{\mu}(S)=\mu/\sqrt{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. The fitted curves exhibit close agreement with the theoretical prediction, thereby validating the asymptotic rate suggested by our bound.
Final test accuracies for both datasets are summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T3.fig1" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.1 A test on the influence of training sample size 𝑆 ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The results further confirm that the generalization error decreases as the number of training samples increases.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20921v1/test_loss_and_predicted_func.png" id="S5.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:447/247;" width="447" height="247" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Average testing-training loss gap of ResNets with <math id="S5.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T,L)=(6,6),(6,24)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T,L)=(6,6),(6,24)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T,L)=(8,8),(8,32)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T,L)=(8,8),(8,32)</annotation></semantics></math> at last 10 epochs versus training sample size <math id="S5.F1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, along with least-squares fitting using <math id="S5.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mu}(S)=\mu/\sqrt{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mu}(S)=\mu/\sqrt{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Plots (a1)-(a4) show results of ResNets on MNIST.
Plots (b1)-(b4) show results of ResNets on CIFAR10.
Plots (c1)-(c4) show results of ResNets on CIFAR100.
The generalization gap decreases with increasing <math id="S5.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, closely matching the theoretical rate of <math id="S5.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\sqrt{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>S</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\sqrt{S})</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S5.T3.fig1" class="ltx_table ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>
The top-1 image classification testing accuracy by trained ResNets with <math id="S5.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T,L)=(6,6),(6,24)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T,L)=(6,6),(6,24)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(T,L)=(8,8),(8,32)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(T,L)=(8,8),(8,32)</annotation></semantics></math> on MNIST, CIFAR10 and CIFAR100 datasets with different training sample sizes <math id="S5.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T3.fig1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T3.fig1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T3.fig1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle ltx_border_tt" colspan="7">Testing accuracy</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:34.1pt;">
<span id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">(T, L)</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:51.2pt;">
<span id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Samples</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_middle ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_middle" style="width:42.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T3.fig1.2.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span></td>
