<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>A test on the layer number of ResNets</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 5. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 Main results and application ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> reveal how the generalization bounds behave as the depth of ResNets increases.
To empirically validate these theoretical results, we conduct experiments by progressively increasing the layer number <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> of the ResNets. The training loss and testing classification accuracy over epochs are plotted in Figure <a href="#S5.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 5.2 A test on the layer number of ResNets ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Figure <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.2 A test on the layer number of ResNets ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ On the Generalization Behavior of Deep Residual Networks From a Dynamical System Perspective" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, respectively.
The results show that as <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> increases, both training loss and testing accuracy of the discrete-time ResNet tend to converge. This empirical behavior is consistent with the theoretical predictions, supporting the connection between network depth, convergence, and generalization performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S5.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.20921v1/T_3_deeplimit_MNIST.png" id="S5.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/86;" width="143" height="86" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F2.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S5.F2.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">MNIST</span></figcaption>
