<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F2.sf6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(f)</span> </span><span id="S5.F2.sf6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">CIFAR100</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span> Training loss of ResNets with varying layer numbers in the deep-layer limit regime.
The first row corresponds to <math id="S5.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=6</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=3,6,12,24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=3,6,12,24</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second row corresponds to <math id="S5.F2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=8</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.F2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=4,8,16,32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=4,8,16,32</annotation></semantics></math>.
Across all datasets (MNIST, CIFAR10, CIFAR100), the training loss exhibits convergence behavior as the number of layers increases, supporting the depth-stability predicted by our theoretical analysis.</figcaption>
</figure>
